  "aliases": [
    "Hos",
    "Ho"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:hosea:12:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Ephraim feedeth on wind, and followeth after the east wind: he daily increaseth lies and desolation; and they do make a covenant with the Assyrians, and oil is carried into Egypt.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hosea 12:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hosea:12:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:hosea:12:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "The LORD hath also a controversy with Judah, and will punish Jacob according to his ways; according to his doings will he recompense him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hosea 12:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hosea:12:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:hosea:12:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "He took his brother by the heel in the womb, and by his strength he had power with God:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hosea 12:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hosea:12:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:hosea:12:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Yea, he had power over the angel, and prevailed: he wept, and made supplication unto him: he found him in Bethel, and there he spake with us;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hosea 12:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hosea:12:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:hosea:12:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Even the LORD God of hosts; the LORD is his memorial.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hosea 12:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hosea:12:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:hosea:12:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Therefore turn thou to thy God: keep mercy and judgment, and wait on thy God continually.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hosea 12:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hosea:12:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:hosea:12:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "He is a merchant, the balances of deceit are in his hand: he loveth to oppress.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hosea 12:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hosea:12:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:hosea:12:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "And Ephraim said, Yet I am become rich, I have found me out substance: in all my labours they shall find none iniquity in me that were sin.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hosea 12:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hosea:12:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:hosea:12:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "And I that am the LORD thy God from the land of Egypt will yet make thee to dwell in tabernacles, as in the days of the solemn feast.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hosea 12:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hosea:12:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:hosea:12:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "I have also spoken by the prophets, and I have multiplied visions, and used similitudes, by the ministry of the prophets.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hosea 12:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hosea:12:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:hosea:12:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Is there iniquity in Gilead? surely they are vanity: they sacrifice bullocks in Gilgal; yea, their altars are as heaps in the furrows of the fields.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hosea 12:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hosea:12:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:hosea:12:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "And Jacob fled into the country of Syria, and Israel served for a wife, and for a wife he kept sheep.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hosea 12:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hosea:12:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:hosea:12:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "And by a prophet the LORD brought Israel out of Egypt, and by a prophet was he preserved.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hosea 12:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hosea:12:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:hosea:12:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Ephraim provoked him to anger most bitterly: therefore shall he leave his blood upon him, and his reproach shall his LORD return unto him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hosea 12:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hosea:12:14"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
    "repository": "aruljohn/Bible-kjv",
